\section{A 3-DOF Tractor Seat-Operator Model.}\label{sec-C}

The model equations are
\begin{equation}\label{3D}
\begin{split}
M_1\ddot{z}_1&+C_1\dot{z}_1+K_1z_1-C_2(\dot{z}_2-\dot{z}_1)-K_2(z_2-z_1)=0,\\
M_2\ddot{z}_2&+C_2(\dot{z}_2-\dot{z}_1)+K_2(z_2-z_1)-C_3(\dot{z}_3-\dot{z}_2)-K_3(z_3-z_2)=0,\\
M_3\ddot{z}_3&-C_3(\dot{z}_3-\dot{z}_2)-K_3(z_3-z_2)=0,
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where $z_1$, $z_2$, $z_3$ denote the displacement of seat mass, of operator pelvis mass, and of thorax and head mass (m). The symbols $M_1$, $M_2$, $M_3$ denote the seat mass, operator pelvis mass, and operator thorax and head mass (kg). The coefficients $K_1$,$K_2$, $K_3$ are spring constant of suspension spring, of cushion material, and of pelvis-thorax connection (N/m). The symbols $C_1$, $C_2$, $C_3$ denote the damping coefficient of suspension damper, of cushion material, and of pelvis-thorax connection (N-s/m).


