\subsection{Trajectory Optimizer}
\label{subsection:trajectory-optimizer}

We separate position and velocity control to simplify the reinforcement learning (RL) model. The RL model focuses on learning the position trajectory, 
\begin{equation}
    \tau_{\text{RL-generated}} = \{ \mathbf{x}_{q,i}^{d} \mid i = 0, \dots, n \},
\end{equation}
%
which reduces the complexity by limiting the state space to positions. This allows the RL algorithm to focus on spatial goals, improving convergence without balancing position and velocity during training.

Once the RL model generates the position trajectory, the Trajectory Optimizer processes the position data to compute the corresponding velocity profile, resulting in
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:computed-trajectory}
\tau_{\text{computed}} = \{ (\mathbf{x}_{q,i}^{d}, \dot{\mathbf{x}}_{q,i}^{d}) \mid i = 0, \dots, n \}.
\end{equation}

This process, detailed in Algorithm~\ref{algo:trajectory-optimization}, we optimize trajectories by smoothing acceleration and deceleration. we iteratively update the velocity profile, constraining it with \(a_{\text{max}}\), which reflect the quadrotor's physical properties, and \(\dot{x}_q^{\text{req}}\), derived in (\ref{eq:velocity-to-achieve-manouvre}), to ensure sufficient energy for the maneuver. By decoupling position and velocity, we enable flexible adjustments to the velocity profile without requiring RL model retraining. Finally, we output \(\tau_{\text{computed}}\), which includes position and velocity at each step, ensuring a smooth stop at the final waypoint.



% a_max -> drone specs, x_max (\dot{x}_q^{\text{req}}) from the calculation (above) -> not used (after revision)

    \begin{algorithm}
\caption{Trajectory Optimization for RL-Generated Trajectory}
\label{algo:trajectory-optimization}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\State Initialize: $\dot{\mathbf{x}}_{q,0}^{d} = 0$
\For{$i = 1$ to $n$}
    \State $\Delta = \|\mathbf{x}_{q,i}^{d} - \mathbf{x}_{q,i-1}^{d}\|$
    \State $\dot{\mathbf{x}}_{q,i}^{d} = \min\left(\dot{\mathbf{x}}_{q,i-1}^{d} + a_{\text{max}} \cdot \Delta t, \dot{x}_q^{\text{req}}\right)$
    \If{$i = n$}
        \State $\dot{\mathbf{x}}_{q,i}^{d} = \min\left(\dot{\mathbf{x}}_{q,i}^{d}, \sqrt{2 \cdot a_{\text{max}} \cdot \Delta}\right)$
    \EndIf
\EndFor
\State \Return $\tau_{\text{computed}} = \{ (\mathbf{x}_{q,i}^{d}, \dot{\mathbf{x}}_{q,i}^{d}) \mid i = 0, \dots, n \}$
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

