	We established verifiable conductance bounds for systematic-scan and random-scan Gibbs samplers over a broad class of target distributions, particularly those satisfying a Poincaré or log-Sobolev inequality and possessing sufficiently regular conditional distributions (Theorem \ref{thm:condss} and Corollary \ref{cor:condrs}). 	
	These bounds directly provide estimates on the mixing time in total variation distance and remain valid for either log-Lipschitz or log-smooth target distributions.
	%This extends previous results beyond log-concave settings \citep{ascolani2024entropy, wadia2024mixing}. 
