\subsection{Generation of Valid SVAs}

\lasa~leverages pre-trained LLMs to generate equivalent assertions for all non-vacuous properties that pass the vacuity check. We found most of the properties were directly translatable into SVAs (refer to Table \ref{tab:performance}) while some posed challenges for direct conversion due to the dependence on the formulation of properties. There were some manual efforts involved for those properties requiring re-prompting for conversion to SVAs. LLMs often struggle with generating correct SVAs due to limited understanding of hardware behavior, signal timing, and implication semantics (e.g., overlapping vs. non-overlapping), etc. LLMs may generate SVAs that are syntactically valid but semantically incorrect such as using non-boolean expressions in implication, incorrect signal scopes, or violating reset behavior constraints. \lasa~integrates verification through Cadence JasperGold and discards the syntactically incorrect or semantically invalid SVAs. 

