A key concept for labeled combinatorial structures is their exponential generating function (EGF for short) defined as $ A(t) = \sum_{n = 0}^{\infty}{\sum_{\alpha \in \mathcal{A}_n}{\frac{w(\alpha)t^n}{n!}}} = \sum_{n=0}^\infty{{a_n}\frac{t^n}{n!}}$. These exponential generating functions encode the relationships between combinatorial structures (i.e., how they are composed). We can write the following relations.

