\begin{proposition}For any distribution $\Omega$, we have $    f_k(n) = \sum_{\tau \in F_{k,n}} w(\tau) \sgn(\tau)$.
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
This follows directly from the expansion $\det A =  \sum_{\pi \in F_n} \sgn(\pi) \prod_{i \in \left[n\right]} A_{i \pi(i)}$ raised to the $k$-th power and by taking expectation as $f_k(n) = \Exx \left[(\det A)^k\right]$.
\end{proof}

