\subsection{Marked permutations and tables}

%\subsection{Shifted basis}
Instead of expressing $f_k(n)$ in terms of $m_r$, we can express it in terms of $\mu_r = \Exx [B_{ij}^r]$ where $B_{ij} = A_{ij} - m_1$.

%there exists another basis which turns out to be much more convenient.
%\begin{definition}
%Let $B_{ij} = A_{ij} - m_1$ with moments $\mu_r = \Exx B_{ij}^r$.
