The key idea is that permutation tables $\mathcal{F}_6^*$ can be decomposed into several components. 
\begin{enumerate}
\item Known $6$-columns, composed as $\textsc{Set}\big{(}(m_6 - 15) \,\, \oneincirc \,\big{)}$ with EGF equal to
\begin{equation*}
e^{(m_6-15)t}.
\end{equation*}
%\item Known $4$-columns where the other two elements of the column are the same element. The EGF for this part is $\textsc{Set}\left(15(m_4 - 3) \,\,
