" (see the introduction). I do not think this adds any new knowledge}

\paragraph*{Software Optimization as a Systems Problem}
A key insight from our study is that performance optimization must be treated as a systems-level task. Instead of isolated rewrites, we view software as an interconnected system where performance emerges from interactions across computation, memory, parallelism, and I/O. Effective optimization spans both high-level architecture and low-level runtime behavior, as shown in our evaluation from microbenchmarks to full applications. We distinguish software systems (modular programs) from computer systems (hardware and runtime), and argue that bridging these layers—by combining structural insights with hardware-level sigonals—is essential for whole-system improvement.
