We now apply a periodic perturbation to the inward propagating ring wave. Above some critical wavelength the perturbations do not grow relative the radial convergence and lower than this critical value the perturbations do grow \citep{OS}. Taking the initial condition
\begin{eqnarray}
 \eta(t_0,x,y) &=& 2v \left(1 + \alpha \cos \left( \beta \arctan \frac{y}{x} \right)\right) \operatorname{sech}^2\left( \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{6v} \left[\sqrt{x^2 + y^2} - (1 + \epsilon v)t_0 - x_0 \right] \right),  \\
u(t_0,x,y) &=& -\frac{x}{\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}} ~ \eta(t_0,x,y), \\
v(t_0,x,y) &=& -\frac{y}{\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}} ~ \eta(t_0,x,y),
\end{eqnarray}
and solving the 2D Boussinesq system gives figure \ref{Inward_ring_periodic}.
