We show that the difference $s_{K_4}(G)-s_{o}(G)$ is arbitrarily large according to the order of a plane triangulation $G$.
To see this,
we construct a plane triangulation $D_k$ 
such that $s_{K_4}(D_k) \ge \frac{12(|V(D_k)|-1)}{20}$ and $s_{o}(D_k) \le \frac{23(|V(D_k)|-1)}{40}$.

