and other two vertices adjacent to $v_c$
together with $x_{j,1},x_{j,2},x_{j,3}$
do not contain any $K_4$-minor
(since the induced subgraph is obtained from a triangle $x_{j,1}x_{j,2}x_{j,3}$ by adding a vertex of degree~2 repeatedly).
Let $W_j$ be the set of such nine vertices in total,
and let $W = \bigcup_{1 \le i \le k} W_i$.
Since the whole induced subgraph $Q = D_k[V(M) \cup W]$ is a $K_4$-minor free graph,
we have $s_{K_4}(D_k) \ge |V(Q)| = 12k$.
Therefore, 
the difference $s_{K_4}(D_k) - s_o(D_k)$ is arbitrarily large according to the order of the triangulation.
This completes the proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:diff_K_4-o}.



