The degree of shrinkage differs across stroke categories. We observe the most aggressive shrinkage in putting, followed by approach shots, with driving skill exhibiting the least shrinkage. This pattern is consistent with the lower signal-to-noise ratio and tighter skill distribution in putting compared to other stroke types.

